<p>The British military parachuted a specialist team and emergency medical supplies onto Tristan da Cunha on Saturday to support a British national with a suspected case of hantavirus in the South Atlantic territory. UK health authorities and reports linked the case to the MV Hondius cruise ship outbreak. The mission used RAF transport aircraft and army medical personnel to reach the isolated British overseas territory. Defence officials released operational details on Sunday after the Saturday drop.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JAnoERM9Ni6BfTDBOYRLDKbXn9rI2VvIIFmzceeWIhVhme1fb2KWxrY7uQE11MY0rea-jfo_QJISuKPZ1YZQPwRXFFq3EN5jMPRTLQSrOw' alt='An ICU nurse and a paratrooper from 16 Air Assault Brigade jump to provide medical support after a suspected hantavirus case on Tristan da Cunha.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Long route: The RAF A400M flew 6,788 km from RAF Brize Norton to Ascension Island and then about 3,000 km south to Tristan da Cunha.</li><li>Mid-air support: An RAF Voyager refuelled the A400M during the mission.</li><li>Landing conditions: An army commander described the landing zone as a “golf course covered in rocks” during the parachute operation.</li></ul><blockquote>With oxygen supplies on the island at a critical level, an airdrop with medical personnel was the only method of getting vital care to the patient in time - UK Ministry of Defence</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UK Ministry of Defence: The ministry said the mission was a landmark use of parachute-delivered military medical personnel for humanitarian support. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458783/british-paratroopers-lead-airdrop-onto-tristan-da-cunha-for-suspected-hantavirus-case'>Aaj TV</a>)</li><li>UK Health Security Agency: The agency confirmed on Friday that a British national had disembarked from the MV Hondius and returned to Tristan da Cunha, where they live. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/10/paratroopers-britain-overseas-territory-suspected-hantavirus-case'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>World Health Organization: The WHO said the patient was stable and had been placed in isolation. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458783/british-paratroopers-lead-airdrop-onto-tristan-da-cunha-for-suspected-hantavirus-case'>Aaj TV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3353102/paratroopers-jump-britains-most-remote-inhabited-island-hantavirus-mission'>Paratroopers jump onto Britain’s most remote inhabited island for hantavirus mission</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/05/10/british-paratroopers-drop-onto-tristan-da-cunha-to-treat-suspected-hantavirus-case'>British paratroopers drop onto Tristan da Cunha to treat suspected hantavirus case</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/05/10/uk-army-parachutes-onto-remote-atlantic-island-over-suspected-hantavirus-case'>UK Army parachutes onto remote Atlantic island over suspected hantavirus case</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgzv77ldpdo'>Army parachutes onto remote island to help Briton with suspected hantavirus</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639846-british-parachute-hantavirus-island/'>British army parachutes hantavirus response team to remote island (VIDEO)</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/british-paratroopers-jump-onto-island-in-hantavirus-response/'>British paratroopers jump onto island in Hantavirus response</a> - ukdefencejournal.org.uk</li><li><a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458783/british-paratroopers-lead-airdrop-onto-tristan-da-cunha-for-suspected-hantavirus-case'>British paratroopers lead airdrop onto Tristan da Cunha for suspected hantavirus case</a> - aaj.tv</li><li><a href='https://www.perthnow.com.au/news/disaster-and-emergency/uk-paratroopers-drop-into-remote-island-over-hantavirus-c-22263065'>UK paratroopers drop into remote 